markp@microsoft.com (Mark Pennington) writes:

|I'm playing a rogue.  My god just granted me Stormy (+1, blessed and
|rustproof).  I decided to see if I could do him a couple better and
|whipped out my blessed wand of wishes.  First I wished for The blessed
|rustproof +20 Stormbringer.  I got a blessed, rustproof broadsword named
|stormbringer.  +20 blade, but no drain.
|Then I wished for a blessed rustproof +20 runed broadsword named Stormbringer.
|After I did an identify on it, it still wasn't THE Stormbringer...no drain.

The problem is that you already have "the" Stormbringer.  There is only one
so you can't wish for another one.  I'm surprised it actually gave you a
+20 anything though!

(spoiler, I guess)

I got one when I sacrificed a bunch of monsters at an altar, but it wasn't
rustproof or +1.  Either way, I like the Vorpal Blade I also have.  I like
the decapitation feature better than SB's draining.  SB also lets you kill
peaceful monsters without asking.  This would be fine, but even a chaotic
character gets penalized by your god for doing that (shouldn't be that way
for chaotic, IMHO).

I've also tried Mjollnir, but it still seems that things get killed quicker
with Vorpal Blade.  Mjollnir also didn't come back to me when I threw it
(with Gauntlets of Power on) like a boomerang like I heard it did.

What's the best artifact weapon to wish for if you don't have one already?

